## 4. Architecture overview

### 4.1 Wrapper scripts

Eight root-owned scripts at `/usr/local/libexec/mythos/`, mode 0755,
owner root:root:

| Wrapper | Purpose | Arguments |
|---|---|---|
| `mythos-servicectl` | systemctl on approved units | `<action> [unit]` |
| `mythos-install-unit` | Deploy systemd unit file | `<basename.service\|timer>` |
| `mythos-install-cloudflared-config` | Deploy cloudflared config | none |
| `mythos-fix-ownership` | Recursive chown /opt/mythos | none |
| `mythos-scan-perms` | Count non-adge-owned files | none |
| `mythos-backup-git` | Create .git/ tar.gz in /tmp | none |
| `mythos-clean-tmp-pack` | Remove stale tmp_pack_* | none |
| `mythos-allowlist-append` | Append unit to allowed-units.txt | `<unit>` |

### 4.2 Configuration file

`/etc/mythos/allowed-units.txt` — root-owned (0644), plain text, one
unit name per line, comments with `#`, blank lines ignored.

Initial content:
```
# Mythos allowed-units list
# Managed by SYS patches. Root-owned. Read by mythos-servicectl.
# One unit name per line. Blank lines and # comments ignored.
# To add a unit: use mythos-allowlist-append, or ship a SYS patch that
# updates this file via the wrapper.

mythos-bot.service
mythos-api.service
mythos-patch-monitor.service
mythos-jupyter.service
cloudflared.service
```

### 4.3 Sudoers drop-in

`/etc/sudoers.d/mythos-patches` — root-owned (0440):

```sudoers
# /etc/sudoers.d/mythos-patches
# Installed by SYS-0063. Do not edit manually.
# Validated with visudo -c before install.
#
# Each entry points at a root-owned wrapper script that validates
# its own arguments. The wrapper is the security boundary, not sudoers.

adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-servicectl *
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-install-unit *
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-install-cloudflared-config
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-fix-ownership
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-scan-perms
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-backup-git
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-clean-tmp-pack
adge ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/libexec/mythos/mythos-allowlist-append *
```

Eight lines. Three have trailing wildcards (servicectl, install-unit,
allowlist-append) because those wrappers take arguments. The wrappers
themselves do all argument validation; sudoers never parses user input.

