### 11.6 ARCHITECTURE.md updates

Add a new section:

```markdown
## Privilege Model

Mythos patches perform privileged operations (systemctl, chown, install
to /etc/) via root-owned wrapper scripts at `/usr/local/libexec/mythos/`.
A narrow sudoers drop-in at `/etc/sudoers.d/mythos-patches` whitelists
only those wrappers. The wrapper scripts do all argument validation;
sudoers never sees user input.

### Wrappers

Located at `/usr/local/libexec/mythos/`, mode 0755, owner root:root:

- `mythos-servicectl <action> <unit>` — systemctl operations on approved units
- `mythos-install-unit <basename>` — deploy systemd unit file
- `mythos-install-cloudflared-config` — deploy cloudflared config
- `mythos-fix-ownership` — recursive chown /opt/mythos to adge:adge
- `mythos-scan-perms [--verbose]` — count non-adge-owned files
- `mythos-backup-git` — create timestamped .git/ backup in /tmp
- `mythos-clean-tmp-pack` — remove stale tmp_pack_* files
- `mythos-allowlist-append <unit>` — add unit to allowed-units.txt

### Allowlist file

`/etc/mythos/allowed-units.txt` — root-owned (0644), plain text, one
unit per line. Read by `mythos-servicectl` to determine which services
can be managed. Updated via `mythos-allowlist-append` or by shipping a
patch that calls `patch.allowlist_append_unit()`.

### Patch framework integration

`PatchBase` exposes privileged operations via convenience methods:

- `patch.restart_service(unit)` → mythos-servicectl restart
- `patch.install_systemd_unit(basename)` → mythos-install-unit
- `patch.scan_perms()` → mythos-scan-perms (returns int)
- `patch.fix_ownership()` → mythos-fix-ownership
- `patch.backup_git()` → mythos-backup-git (returns path)
- `patch.allowlist_append_unit(unit)` → mythos-allowlist-append

Under the hood all these call `patch.sudo_wrapper(wrapper_name, *args)`
which invokes `sudo -n /usr/local/libexec/mythos/<wrapper>`. Because the
wrappers are whitelisted in sudoers for passwordless invocation by adge,
this works without prompting for a password in both interactive terminals
and monitor-triggered (no-TTY) installs.

### Installed by SYS-0063 and SYS-0064

- SYS-0063: installs the wrappers + sudoers + allowlist
- SYS-0064: updates patch_base.py to use the wrappers
```

