## 14. Unresolved / optional improvements

These are nice-to-haves but not required for the plan to succeed.
Punt to future patches unless specifically requested.

### 14.1 Hash verification of wrappers

SYS-0063 could embed expected SHA-256 hashes for each wrapper and
verify them post-install. Adds complexity in exchange for tamper
detection. Skipped for now.

### 14.2 selinux / AppArmor compatibility

Ubuntu 24.04 has AppArmor enabled by default. Haven't checked whether
any AppArmor profile interferes with the wrappers. Should be fine
because `/usr/local/libexec/` isn't typically covered by profiles,
but worth checking with `aa-status` during the fresh conversation if
anything acts weird.

### 14.3 Logging

Wrappers don't log their invocations anywhere. Could add syslog writes
for audit trail. Not in scope for SYS-0063. Future hardening.

### 14.4 Automatic wrapper updates

If a future patch changes a wrapper script, it needs to ship the new
wrapper AND use `sudo install` to replace the old one. No mechanism
exists to automate this. Probably fine for now — wrapper changes should
be rare and deliberate.

### 14.5 Bootstrap using systemd one-shot service instead of interactive sudo

SYS-0063 currently requires interactive sudo for its own bootstrap.
An alternative would be to ship SYS-0063 as a systemd one-shot service
that runs as root, does the install, then removes itself. More
engineering, but completely eliminates the interactive sudo step.

Not worth it — the one-time bootstrap requirement is a small price
and the monitor-triggered case is handled by the TTY check.

